  {
    "episode_id": 86581,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86581.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "I don't believe there's a waiting period. Most of the provisions of this will go into effect right away. There are also provisions at the state level that need to be put into place. And in fact, I've spoken very recently with our House leadership to make sure I'm hoping that Missouri will be one of the very first states to have a companion piece of legislation at the state level so that the attorneys general and others can use that. to also prosecute. You know, most of the prosecutions do happen at the state and local level. So it's important that we get the states on board. As I said, 50 state attorneys general have asked us to put this legislation forward. So I want to get it, once it's signed by the president, I want to get it as quickly to the Missouri State General Assembly as possible.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
