  {
    "episode_id": 86581,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86581.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Now, while you're in Jeff's city, in fact, I was in Jeff's city this week too, we kind of crossed paths, but you got at least two active Democratic opponents in your district, in the second district. Obviously, you're in incumbent, you've got a lot of connections, you've been successful raising money, Obviously, you would have an advantage in there. But still, this is rare. I mean, for the Democrats, your last two elections, you did not have as strong candidates or at least candidates who weren't able to tap into some money. I mean, the DCCC has already been sending out little missives about you, attacks, this and that. How do you see the climate this time as you're running for reelection differ or not from the last couple times?",
