  {
    "episode_id": 86581,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86581.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "always get them. You know, in Missouri, it's a $100 filing fee. A lot of people file for office. And, you know, I intend on taking this election seriously. I take every election seriously and work hard and earn the vote. This is a district that's personal for me. I'm born and raised here in the St. Louis Metro area. Raised my family of three. My husband and I have been married for 31 years. We've worked. We've volunteered. We've done a lot in this community and it's personal. This for me, Joe, is a calling, not a job. And I am here to serve the people of the second district. It's an honor and a privilege. And I think that every candidate, the key to success is to focus on your constituents. And I talk about the things that we do for my constituents back home, whether that's fighting for the NGA here, which is jobs, whether it's lifting our defense appropriations and making sure that that Boeing line has got increased numbers of growlers and super hornets. Whether it's fighting for a strong sex trafficking legislation, you know, St. Louis, sadly, is in the top 20 on sex trafficking in our nation. So we do a lot with the VA. I have the privilege of having Jefferson Barracks in the district, a lot in terms of constituent services with a strong district office. So the key to any election and any candidate I think being elected in their district is how hard you work to deliver for the people that you represent. So you can't ever stop coming home. You can't ever stop. I always say I'm Ann Wagner of Baldwin, not of Washington and the Imperial City. I am much more at home here in the second district and in my home of decades out in in Baldwin, Missouri. So we're going to work hard. I take it seriously. It's a tough climate. And we are targeted by the DCCC. So I'll take nothing for granted.",
