    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86581.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 42,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm a big team player and I believe that if I work hard and do what I need to do to turn out the votes in the second district, that we lift all votes. And one of the discussions that I had with my colleagues in the General Assembly, who I work very closely with, both in the Missouri House and Senate, is what I can do to help those state reps and those state senators that are in Missouri's second district. So I will work hand in hand with them, whether it's out knocking doors, whether it's through helping them raise the resources that they need, campaign strategy. My staff is available on the political side to work with them. I've always been a party player and a team player here, so that will not change. And I think we'll have the resources to get our message out. And because we work so hard, and in terms of taking these elections, Seriously, I do think that it is of benefit to the other campaigns too. They may be newer to the political process or to the campaign side of things. So whatever we can do to be of assistance, I will be there no matter what.",
