  {
    "episode_id": 86581,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86581.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 48,
    "turn_text": "Well, we got our budget deal several weeks ago, and now we are going to be working with the appropriators and passing our full budget funding that will happen at the end of March. So I've been finding a lot for our defense dollars and to make sure that we as a country are safe and secure and that our readiness is intact and putting the kind of money that we need to into. the Defense Department, whether that's the VA, whether that's giving our soldiers a much needed pay raise, whether that's more super hornets and growlers on the assembly line or Navy carriers, whatever it is, we need to make sure that our warfighters are ready to keep us safe and secure. So we're going to be working on our funding bills. I serve on the Financial Services Committee, and the Senate has finally decided to move a package of regulatory reform issues when it comes to community banks and other financial service sector agencies that will be taking up in the House. We passed our version, the Choice Act. months and months ago, but they are finally going to move on a package and I'm thrilled to be able to move that forward. One of the big successes I think of this administration has been to take the blanket off of businesses and enterprises and companies and individuals restore their freedoms and have the kind of regulatory reform that we've seen that has really, I think, been a part of jump-starting this economy. We passed historic tax cuts and jobs growth act that is beginning to see the benefits now, not just in growth in our GDP, but in real people's paychecks and pocketbooks. So we're thrilled that that the consumer confidence has grown. Small businesses are expanding and buying the equipment, growing their warehouses, their workforces. It's not just about giving bonuses, which are terrific. It's about increasing their pay and growing their businesses. So whether it's regulatory reform, the tax reform package that we had go through, certainly the defense dollars are why ISIS is on the run. And we're going to be working on a number of these issues. I'm also on Foreign Affairs, so I have an on the Asia-Pacific Subcommittee and have been very involved in our dealings with the North Koreans and in the Korean Peninsula. I have visited the region in South Korea, in China, in Japan, and have been very involved in the work on Foreign Affairs. There is plenty on our plate and a lot more to be done. I do hope that we're going to be able to take action on this legislation. We've got a number of pieces that have passed through the House. The Senate moves way too slow for my... for my liking, but I do hope that they're going to pass my FOSTA bill and the Fight Online Sex Trafficking Act and that they'll be able to get to some of the other items that we have moved to their chamber and can hopefully make it to the President's desk.",
