    "turn_text": "you know, I care deeply about the debt and what we're passing along to our children. And now I'm a brand new first-time grandma. And what my little granddaughter Isabella Marie may have to deal with. So these are important issues. One of the only reasons that I supported some of these increases is that I do believe that we are going to see real growth in our gross domestic product and that that will be a real catalyst to going after our debt in deficit. I believe in the dynamic scoring process and I'm hopeful that whether it's through regulatory relief that has allowed this economic boom and growth and consumer confidence and manufacturing expansion or whether it's through the tax cut plan that our GDP will grow, our economy will grow. Real people are going to have more discretionary dollars of their own money that they'll be able to spend and that that will be a real driver. Just one point increase in the GDP really does an amazing amount of difference to our debt and deficits. But I continue to be a budget hawk and have real concerns about our spending going forward.",
